5. Why the privacy-shutter plant test cannot catch a missing tile

  test_plant_leaving_one_sensory_tile_out_fails (test_shellmodel.py:179) does
  this:

      planted_model = ShellModel(demand_store=self.demand_store)
      planted_model.refresh_state()
      planted_model.microphone_tile.shutter_closed = False
      planted_model.microphone_tile.label = "Microphone: STANDBY"
      with self.assertRaises(AssertionError):
          verify_shutter_coverage(planted_model)

  The "plant" is performed by hand on the tile, after refresh_state has already
  run, and the assertion is on the test's own helper verify_shutter_coverage.
  It proves that the helper raises when a tile is wrong. It never exercises
  ShellModel at all: no model ever runs its refresh path with a tile omitted, so
  S17-P1's omission stays green. Meanwhile
  test_privacy_shutter_closed_shown_on_every_sensory_tile iterates
  model.get_sensory_tiles(), which is the same list the model uses to refresh —
  if a tile were dropped from both, the loop would simply check one fewer tile.

  F3.15-F2 (finding): the plant test is written against the checker, not the
  subject. The queue asked for "a plant that leaves one tile out"; to meet that
  the test must construct a model whose refresh path omits a tile and assert
  that the invariant check fails. Today the omission is invisible, which is
  exactly the "checker shares its subject's assumptions" failure AGENTS.md
  opens with.

