6. A3.13's committed evidence, docs/logs/e5-no-tkinter.log

  The file is UTF-16LE with CRLF, so git stores it as binary:

  $ git show 0ff754f --stat -- docs/logs/e5-no-tkinter.log
   docs/logs/e5-no-tkinter.log | Bin 0 -> 49758 bytes
   1 file changed, 0 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-)

  $ file docs/logs/e5-no-tkinter.log
  docs/logs/e5-no-tkinter.log: Unicode text, UTF-16, little-endian text, with CRLF line terminators

  Decoded, the content is real and supports the claim. It is a PowerShell
  transcript (the "+ CategoryInfo"/"At line:1 char:1" noise is PowerShell
  echoing stderr), it ran the whole suite with tkinter blocked, and it shows the
  two GUI skips plus the import test passing:

  Ran 134 tests in 3193.700s
  OK (skipped=4)

  test_shellgui_import_does_not_require_tkinter ... ok
  GUI smoke test verifies ShellGUI initializes, and SKIPs loudly when no display exists. ... skipped 'SKIP LOUDLY: Graphical display unavailable: import of tkinter halted; None in sys.modules'

  F3.15-F3 (finding, low): the evidence is honest but unreadable in the repo.
  `git show`, `git log -p` and GitHub's diff all say "Binary files differ", so a
  reviewer cannot read the log that is supposed to prove the claim. Re-record it
  as UTF-8 (on PowerShell: `... | Out-File -Encoding utf8`), or set
  `$OutputEncoding` and pipe through `Set-Content -Encoding utf8`.

