  That A3.13 log says the blocked-tkinter run took 3193.7 seconds (53 minutes)
  for 134 tests. The same suite on the CI image takes about six seconds. On this
  host, running the blocked full suite stalls on one test:

  $ timeout 150 python -u -c "import sys; sys.modules['tkinter']=None; ... discover -s novacore/tests -v" > /tmp/fullblocked.txt 2>&1; echo "exit=$?"
  exit=124
  $ tail -3 /tmp/fullblocked.txt
  test_full_companion_turn_with_stored_memory (test_llm_privacy.LLMPrivacyTests.test_full_companion_turn_with_stored_memory)
  Store a memory with a token, run a full Companion turn, and verify no leak outside memory store. ...

  I did not wait for it to finish, so I cannot say whether it hangs forever or
  is merely very slow (the A3.13 log finishing at 3193 s suggests slow rather
  than hung). test_llm_privacy is not part of A3.13 or A3.17 and I did not
  investigate it; flagging it for whoever owns that module, because "run the
  whole suite locally" is not practical at 53 minutes and reviewers will stop
