VERDICT: FAIL

  Two of the five plants stayed green, and both are the ones the work order
  cares about most: the "plant that leaves one tile out" test does not test the
  model, and the GUI smoke test cannot fail. A3.13's actual fix — lazy tkinter
  import plus the blocked-tkinter verification — is correct and I verified it in
  both directions; the clock, the notification cap and the import guard are all
  genuinely load-bearing. The item fails on the two missed plants, per rule 15,
  not because the shell is broken today.

  WHAT I COULD NOT DO:
    - Measure the full blocked suite to completion (the timeout fired at 150 s
      inside test_llm_privacy). Everything I report for the shell tests was run
      to completion.
    - View the A3.17 GUI visually. I checked that shellgui.py binds both sensory
      tile labels and the notification list to StringVars, and that the smoke
      test constructs a real Tk window here, but nobody looked at the window.
    - Test with a host that has tkinter but no display server. This host has a
      working display, so the skip path I exercised was the blocked-module path,
      which is the one CI takes.

  WHAT I AM UNSURE OF:
    - Whether the owner wants the GUI smoke test to be a real GUI test at all.
      If it is only meant to prove "a window can be opened", then narrowing the
      except is enough; if it is meant to catch regressions, it needs assertions
      on widget content, and there are none.
    - Whether the 53-minute local runtime is a defect in test_llm_privacy or a
      property of this host. I only measured that it exceeds 150 s here.
